// ===================== 10.4 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('10.4  Compared with what?'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **The three questions must be asked in order and all three asked**, even when the first fails: a comparison can fail on period and still be interesting about definition. **In most comparisons at least one of the three fails**, and students will not believe that until they have run the stage on their own work.'));
out.push(A('**b** A reader can use: **2** and **4** — both bases printed, and **4** also names the definition change. Not: **1**, **3** and **5**. ⚠ **1** is the one to read out: _twice as many refusals as last year_ **hides both numbers**, and twice as many can be two against one.'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — **same period? same definition? same population?** — and Mrs Nasser\'s comparison fails **two of the three**: a changed assessment and a selected group of nine against twenty-two. **The period passes.**'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** It obliges you to **say what you held constant** — three named constants, **or do not use the phrase.**   **2** **That the two figures cannot be compared, and what you would need in order to compare them** — which reads as a refusal for about four seconds **and then reads as competence.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The distinction to teach is which fault can be mended: the population question can sometimes be repaired and the definition question never can.** **No quantity converts a written paper into an observed lesson** — and arithmetic is what every student tries first. Mrs Nasser\'s own repair is the model: ⚠ **take last year\'s nine strongest on their written papers and eight of the nine completed** — **which tells you something and is still not a comparison**, because the definition is two different things. **Mark the attempt as correct and the conclusion as wrong**, which is the only way students learn the difference between a repair and a comparison.'));
out.push(NOTE('**The refusal sentence is the deliverable of this cycle and it is worth drilling as a formula, because under pressure nobody invents it.** ⚠ **_These two figures cannot be compared. Here is each with its base. Here is which of the three questions fails. To compare them I should need —, and that will exist in —._** Five parts, and **the date is the part students leave out.** A refusal with a date **turns into a plan**; a refusal without one **gets the same request again in a fortnight** from somebody who did not read the page. ⚠ And tell the class Mrs Khoury\'s observation, because it removes the fear: **no reader has ever thought less of a writer for it**, and many readers discover in that paragraph that **a comparison they had been quoting for two years was never available.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**1** _(two quarters)_ _Nine of forty this quarter, against six of thirty-one last quarter._ **All three pass.**',
  '**2** _(one year incomplete)_ _Nine refusals in nine months this year, against six in twelve months last year — **nine in nine months is twelve a year.** Period fails and is repairable by arithmetic._',
  '**3** _(two groups of different sizes)_ _Seven of nine, against fourteen of twenty-two. Population fails; **partly repairable** by taking last year\'s nine strongest._',
  '**4** _(after a definition changed)_ _Disputes down a quarter since February — **and a dispute was redefined in January.** Definition fails; **not repairable at all.**_',
  '**5** _(cannot be compared)_ _These two figures cannot be compared. Seven of nine, by observed lesson; fourteen of twenty-two, by written paper, and the nine were selected. **To compare them I should need two groups assessed the same way, and the first will exist in June.**_',
]));
out.push(A('⚠ Mark these on **which question fails and whether the fault is repairable**, in two words in the margin: _period, repairable_ · _definition, not_. Item **5** is the one to collect from everybody, and mark it on **the five parts**: both figures with bases, which question fails, what would be needed, **and the date.** The date is missing from most first attempts, **and without it the paragraph is a refusal and not a plan.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
