  '**Because the same forty seconds, at eleven calls an hour over a working year, is about two working days of one person\'s time.** ⚠ **Both numbers are true and they are the same fact**, and I had been giving the small one in three meetings while arguing in favour of the page. I did not notice I was choosing.',
  '**What I did differently was one sentence long.** I now write both sizes together — _forty seconds a call, which is about two working days a year_ — and I have stopped being surprised in meetings. ⚠ **Take the figure you quoted most often last year and work out the other end of it. Twenty seconds.** If the two sizes make you feel differently about your own position, **you have found out something about yourself and not about the form.**',
